(6850483, 1030405, 42013, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Teafran:</b></div><hr/><i> Four times I came back to this image as I couldn''t figure out what was wrong with it. Now I know - the full face is slightly out of focus on one side (our right - her left) - leaves the image unbalanced which is a negative. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Fair observation. f1.8 was making it difficult to fine tune the focus. It was just close enough that i figured it worked in spite of the missed focus on near eye.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Teafran: Four times I came back to this image as I couldn''t figure out what was wrong with it. Now I know - the full face is slightly out of focus on one side (our right - her left) - leaves the image unbalanced which is a negative.   Fair observation. f1.8 was making it difficult to fine tune the focus. It was just close enough that i figured it worked in spite of the missed focus on near eye.', '2012-08-28 02:46:18.000000', NULL, 0),
